CONFLICTS=[
('C1','Preferred schedule versus comparison schedules','Preferred main p.3 anneals S 1 h / Cd 2.5 h; Table 1 has separate S 1 h / Cd 3 h and other schedules. Main p.3 says initial 5–8 cycles then ligand ratio switch; p.6 says more OA starting at the fifth to eighth shell. These are retained as differently worded scopes, without a fabricated exact switch.'),
('C2','Rounded narrative anneal and table QY values','Main p.4 calls the long total anneal 3 h although Table 1 asymmetric schedules include 3 h plus 10 min. Narrative 21±0.2% and 41±6% are distinct summaries, while the table uses approximate/bounded QYs; do not replace either set.'),
('C3','SI secondary-amine caption identity','Figure S6 specifies dioctylamine synthesis but names oleylamine/NH2 in its thin-shell assignment. Main p.6 describes dioctylamine signatures. No identity correction or quantitative surface-ligand coverage is inferred.'),
('C4','Nonblinking inequality','Main p.4 says >99% on-time; Figure 3 says ≥99%. Both remain explicit, with the experimental classification equation and denominator retained.'),
('C5','Approximate versus displayed phase ratio','Table 2 gives secondary-amine ~70:30 WZ:ZB; Figure S4c labels 67:33. Primary-amine S4b is 74:26 and constant sulfur S4d 40:60. These are separate source presentations, not substituted values.'),
('C6','Large-core shell-label join remains unverified','SI S7 and S8 specify 5.5 nm/16.9 ML; Table S1 ends the 5.5 nm sequence at 15.57 ML. The trace examples are not force-joined to that row. Nominal versus TEM-derived layer counts might differ, but the paper does not explicitly resolve the mapping.')]
GAPS=[
('G1','Upstream stocks and reagent details','Cd-oleate and TOP-Se preparation, stock batch volumes, exact dissolved speciation and dioctylamine supplier/grade are absent. CdO and Se/TOP are listed but no unreported precursor preparation reaction is invented.'),
('G2','Practical synthesis and purification missingness','Exact several-minute/second durations, quench temperature/volume, addition rates, centrifugation settings, washing volumes and yields are absent. The 7 nm and still larger control-core preparation is unreported.'),
('G3','Sample joins and variant boundaries','Many TEM/FTIR/XRD population images lack unique batch/core/shell labels. Table series are parameter comparisons, not a complete factorial design. No exact cross-technique or per-row QY/lifetime joins are fabricated.'),
('G4','Per-layer material accounting','Precursor aliquot volumes, exact particle number calibration, layer-by-layer concentration/dilution schedule and exact OA switch cycle are absent. One-percent and ten-percent labels are removed solution fractions, not known molar excesses.'),
('G5','Characterization details','Some concentrations/deposition volumes, QY comparison settings, TEM voltage/grid, exact film thickness and numeric dilution factors are unreported; laser spot/power quantities preserve their approximate scope.'),
('G6','No atomistic product structure','TEM and PXRD support morphology and phase associations; no atomic coordinates, full refined cell constants, CIF, SAED or dipole measurement is provided. The 0.3375 nm ML assumption is not a qualified product structure.'),
('G7','Surface speciation limits','FTIR assignments and proposed ligand binding/termination mechanisms do not establish exact ligand counts, coverage, metal complexes or surface atom positions.'),
('G8','Graph and fit limitations','Figure 3/4 points and uncertainty bars are not digitized into invented precision. SI S1 reports averages of fitted parameters; original fit/trajectory files, exact uncertainties and individual source records are unavailable. The approximately 750 nm³ relationship and ~65 ns trend remain scoped, with the 3.0 nm exception.')]

